---
title: Style guide
layout: layouts/base.njk
contentClass: wide style-guide
hideSignup: true # the sign-up variants are shown in the Forms section instead
eleventyImport:
  collections: ["allPosts", "writing", "notes", "letters", "art", "sketching", "completedBooks"]
---
{#- Dev-only reference for every style and component on the site. Lives in
    src/site/dev/, so it renders at /dev/style-guide/ under `npm start` and is
    never built in production (dev.11tydata.js). Examples use real content
    and the real components/macros, so this page stays in step with the site.
    The page's own scaffolding (swatches, section labels) is styled in the
    <style> block at the bottom, so no extra stylesheet ships with the site.
    Note: the sign-up examples repeat id="bd-email" — fine here, but never
    put two sign-up forms on a real page. #}
{%- from "components/post-card.njk" import postCard %}
{%- from "components/reading/cover.njk" import bookCover %}
{%- from "components/home-cards.njk" import more, storyCard as card %}

<article>
  <header>
    <p class="section-label"><a href="/">&larr; Home</a></p>
    <h1>Style guide</h1>
    <time>Dev only · never published</time>
  </header>

<p>Every style and component on teresawatts.com, for reference. Each section names the template or class to use. Styles live in <code>src/site/styles/</code>: tokens in <code>_tokens.scss</code>, base elements in <code>_base.scss</code>, page frame in <code>_layout.scss</code>, components in <code>_components.scss</code>, and the homepage in <code>_home.scss</code>.</p>

<nav class="sg-toc" aria-label="Sections">
  <a href="#tokens">Tokens</a> <a href="#type">Typography</a> <a href="#post">Post page</a> <a href="#index">Index pages</a> <a href="#lists">Post lists</a> <a href="#reading">Reading</a> <a href="#forms">Forms &amp; sign-up</a> <a href="#home">Homepage</a> <a href="#frame">Nav &amp; footer</a>
</nav>

{#- ============================================================ -#}
<h2 id="tokens" class="sg-h">Design tokens</h2>
<p class="sg-note"><code>_tokens.scss</code>: CSS custom properties, so a reskin can be previewed live in devtools. The main palette, then the supporting colours, each tuned for one job.</p>

<div class="sg-swatches">
  {%- for t in [
    { name: "--color-primary", note: "pink · accents, hover underline" },
    { name: "--color-secondary", note: "blue · links, headings, buttons" },
    { name: "--color-text", note: "grey · body text (7.7:1)" },
    { name: "--color-background", note: "pink-lightest · page" },
    { name: "--color-accent", note: "pink-light · tags, link hover, dividers" }
  ] %}
  <div class="sg-swatch"><span style="background: var({{ t.name }})"></span><code>{{ t.name }}</code><small>{{ t.note }}</small></div>
  {%- endfor %}
  {%- for t in [
    { name: "--color-muted", note: "muted grey · footer text, form field borders (4.8:1 on white)" },
    { name: "--color-label", note: "dark terracotta · homepage card labels (4.6:1)" },
    { name: "--color-wash", note: "white wash · Writing band, sign-up panel" }
  ] %}
  <div class="sg-swatch"><span style="background: var({{ t.name }})"></span><code>{{ t.name }}</code><small>{{ t.note }}</small></div>
  {%- endfor %}
</div>

<div class="sg-fonts">
  <div><p class="sg-font-serif">Newsreader</p><code>--font-family</code><small>body, headings, titles</small></div>
  <div><p class="sg-font-sans">Avenir</p><code>--font-family-sans-serif</code><small>nav, labels, dates, buttons, footer</small></div>
  <div><p class="sg-radius"></p><code>--border-radius: 4px</code><small>images, tags</small></div>
</div>

{#- ============================================================ -#}
<h2 id="type" class="sg-h">Typography</h2>
<p class="sg-note"><code>_base.scss</code>. Inside <code>.content</code> (pages and posts) body text is 1.25rem.</p>

<h1>Heading 1</h1>
<h2>Heading 2</h2>
<h3>Heading 3</h3>
<h4>Heading 4</h4>
<h5>Heading 5</h5>
<h6>Heading 6</h6>

<p>Body paragraph with a <a href="#type">link</a>, some <strong>bold</strong> and <em>italic</em> text, <code>inline code</code>, and an inline <q>quotation</q>. Paragraphs have 1.5rem below them.</p>

<ul>
  <li>Unordered list item</li>
  <li>Another item, with a <a href="#type">link</a></li>
</ul>
<ol>
  <li>Ordered list item</li>
  <li>Second item</li>
</ol>

<blockquote><p>A blockquote: smaller sans text with a pink rule on the left. Used for callouts and quotes in posts.</p></blockquote>

<hr>

<time>A &lt;time&gt; element: sans, block, used for dates</time>

<figure>
  <img src="/img/user/assets/portraitv2.png" alt="Illustrated self-portrait of Teresa Watts" style="width: 160px">
  <figcaption>A figure with a caption (<code>figure figcaption</code>). Images get the 4px radius and centre by default.</figcaption>
</figure>

{#- ============================================================ -#}
<h2 id="post" class="sg-h">Post page</h2>
<p class="sg-note"><code>layouts/post.njk</code>: back link (<code>.section-label</code>), title, date, tags (<code>a.tag</code>), then the body, then previous/next (<code>.post-nav</code>).</p>

<div class="sg-frame">
  <article>
    <header>
      <p class="section-label"><a href="/writing/">&larr; Writing</a></p>
      <h1>A post title</h1>
      <time>Published on 24 September 2026</time>
      <div class="header-tags"><a class="tag" href="/tags/art/">#art</a><a class="tag" href="/tags/letters/">#letters</a></div>
    </header>
    <p>Post body text…</p>
    <nav class="post-nav" aria-label="More in writing">
      <a class="post-nav-prev" href="#post">&larr; Newer post</a>
      <a class="post-nav-next" href="#post">Older post &rarr;</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</div>

{#- ============================================================ -#}
<h2 id="index" class="sg-h">Index pages</h2>
<p class="sg-note"><code>layouts/index.njk</code>: <code>.index-header</code> with a title and optional <code>intro</code>, or <code>titleImage</code> in front matter for a picture heading (the Letters page). Then the post list and <code>.pagination</code>.</p>

<div class="sg-frame">
  <header class="index-header">
    <h1>Writing</h1>
    <p class="index-intro">Longer-form posts about design, art, tools and process.</p>
  </header>
</div>
<div class="sg-frame">
  <header class="index-header">
    <h1 class="index-title-image"><img src="/img/user/assets/Letters.png" alt="Letters from Teresa"></h1>
  </header>
</div>
<div class="sg-frame">
  <nav class="pagination" aria-label="Pagination example">
    <a class="pagination-prev" href="#index">&larr; Newer</a>
    <span class="pagination-status">Page 2 of 5</span>
    <a class="pagination-next" href="#index">Older &rarr;</a>
  </nav>
  <p class="index-empty">Nothing here yet — check back soon. (<code>.index-empty</code>)</p>
</div>

{#- ============================================================ -#}
<h2 id="lists" class="sg-h">Post lists</h2>
<p class="sg-note"><code>components/post-card.njk</code> (<code>postCard</code>) inside <code>ul.post-list</code>, with a <code>listClass</code> per page. Real, current posts.</p>

<h3 class="sg-sub">Writing · <code>.writing-list</code></h3>
<ul class="post-list writing-list">
  {%- for post in collections.writing | head(2) %}{{ postCard(post, { showImage: true, bodyImageFallback: true }) }}{% endfor %}
</ul>

<h3 class="sg-sub">Notes · <code>.notes-list</code></h3>
<ul class="post-list notes-list">
  {%- for post in collections.notes | head(3) %}{{ postCard(post) }}{% endfor %}
</ul>

<h3 class="sg-sub">Letters · <code>.letters-list</code></h3>
<ul class="post-list letters-list">
  {%- for post in collections.letters | head(3) %}{{ postCard(post) }}{% endfor %}
</ul>

<h3 class="sg-sub">Art, sketching, Making · <code>.art-grid</code></h3>
<ul class="post-list art-grid">
  {%- for post in collections.art | head(3) %}{{ postCard(post, { showImage: true }) }}{% endfor %}
</ul>

<h3 class="sg-sub">All posts · <code>.posts-mosaic</code></h3>
<ul class="post-list posts-mosaic">
  {%- for post in collections.allPosts | head(4) %}{{ postCard(post, { showImage: true, showSection: true }) }}{% endfor %}
</ul>

{#- ============================================================ -#}
<h2 id="reading" class="sg-h">Reading</h2>
<p class="sg-note"><code>components/reading/</code>: <code>bookCover</code> in a <code>.cover-grid</code> (with the "Reading" badge for current books, and a text placeholder when there's no cover), and <code>.article-list</code> for saved articles.</p>

<section class="reading-section">
  <ul class="cover-grid">
    {%- for book in "reading" | shelfCards | head(1) %}{{ bookCover(book, true) }}{% endfor %}
    {%- for post in collections.completedBooks | head(3) %}{{ bookCover(post) }}{% endfor %}
    <li><a href="#reading" title="A book with no cover"><span class="cover-placeholder">A book with no cover</span></a></li>
  </ul>
</section>
<section class="reading-section">
  <ul class="article-list">
    <li><a href="#reading">An article I read and liked</a> <span class="reading-meta">example.com · 1 October 2026</span></li>
    <li><a href="#reading">Another saved article</a> <span class="reading-meta">example.org · 12 September 2026</span></li>
  </ul>
</section>

{#- ============================================================ -#}
<h2 id="forms" class="sg-h">Forms &amp; sign-up</h2>
<p class="sg-note">The Buttondown form is <code>.signup-form</code> (visible label, white field with a 4.8:1 outline, blue button; the RSS copy field shares the field and button styles). On its own it's how the Letters page used to look; normally it comes inside the <code>components/letters-signup.njk</code> panel, set with <code>signupLayout</code> and friends (see the component's comment).</p>

<h3 class="sg-sub">Letters panel · two columns (every page, above the footer)</h3>
{%- set signupLayout = "two" %}
{% include "components/letters-signup.njk" %}

<h3 class="sg-sub">Letters panel · stacked (homepage)</h3>
{%- set signupLayout = "stacked" %}
{% include "components/letters-signup.njk" %}

<h3 class="sg-sub">Letters panel · stacked, no lettering or past-letters link (Letters page)</h3>
{%- set signupNoTitle = true %}
{%- set signupNoPast = true %}
{% include "components/letters-signup.njk" %}
{%- set signupNoTitle = false %}
{%- set signupNoPast = false %}

<h3 class="sg-sub">RSS copy field · <code>.rss-copy</code> (/rss/)</h3>
<p class="rss-copy"><input type="text" readonly value="https://teresawatts.com/feed.xml" aria-label="Feed address"><button type="button">Copy</button></p>


</article>

{#- ============================================================ -#}
{#- the homepage's pieces are at its width, so this part breaks out of the
    reading column (.home-main gives them the homepage's links and size) #}
<div class="home-main sg-wide" id="home">
  <h2 class="sg-h">Homepage</h2>
  <p class="sg-note"><code>index.njk</code> + <code>layouts/home.njk</code>, styles in <code>_home.scss</code>. Card macro: <code>storyCard</code> in <code>components/home-cards.njk</code>.</p>

  <h3 class="sg-sub">Intro · <code>.home-intro</code> (<code>components/home-intro.njk</code>)</h3>
  {% include "components/home-intro.njk" %}

  <h3 class="sg-sub">Section title with "View all" · <code>.home-head</code> + <code>more()</code> (<code>.more-link</code>)</h3>
  <header class="home-head"><h2>Making</h2>{{ more("/making/", "View all") }}</header>

  <h3 class="sg-sub">Big story cards in a ratio row · <code>.home-top.ratio-row</code> + <code>.story-card</code></h3>
  <p class="sg-note">Each card grows by its image's width÷height (<code>--r</code>), so the row shares one height and nothing is cropped. Label in dark terracotta; picture lifts on hover.</p>
  <section class="home-top ratio-row">
    {%- for post in collections.allPosts | inSections(["art", "sketching", "sketchbooks"]) | head(2) %}{{ card(post, "", true) }}{% endfor %}
  </section>

  <h3 class="sg-sub">Compact cards · <code>.home-writing-grid</code> in the Writing band (<code>.home-band.is-tint</code>)</h3>
  <section class="home-band is-tint">
    <div class="home-writing-grid">
      {%- for post in collections.allPosts | inSections(["writing", "letters"]) | head(3) %}
      {%- set t = post | cardImageAny %}
      {{- card(post, "is-compact", true, t and not ("Pasted" in t.src), not ("letters" in post.data.section)) }}
      {%- endfor %}
      {%- for post in collections.writing | notInSections(["letters"]) | head(1) %}
      {{- card(post, "is-compact", true, false, true) }}
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <h3 class="sg-sub">Book covers and notes list · <code>.home-pair</code>, <code>.home-covers</code>, <code>.home-notes</code></h3>
  <div class="home-pair">
    <div>
      <div class="home-covers">
        {%- for post in collections.completedBooks | head(3) %}
        {%- set thumb = post | cardImage %}
        <a href="{{ post.url }}" title="{{ post.data.title }}">{% if thumb %}<img src="{{ thumb.src }}" alt="{{ post.data.title }}" loading="lazy"{% if thumb.remote %} eleventy:ignore{% endif %}>{% else %}<span class="home-cover-blank">{{ post.data.title }}</span>{% endif %}</a>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <ul class="home-notes">
        {%- for post in collections.notes | head(3) %}
        <li><a href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title }}</a><span class="home-notes-topic">{{ (post.data.tags or [])[0] }}</span></li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="sg-frame-note" id="frame">
  <h2 class="sg-h">Nav &amp; footer</h2>
  <p class="sg-note">The real ones are on this page: the nav at the top (<code>components/nav.njk</code>, links from <code>site.nav</code> in <code>site.json</code>, <code>also</code> lists extra paths that light a link up) and the footer below (<code>components/footer.njk</code>, links from <code>site.footer</code>, with the dashed cut line and scissors).</p>
</div>

{#- the style guide's own scaffolding (not site styles) #}
<style>
  .style-guide .sg-toc { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.4rem 1rem; margin: 0 0 2rem; font-family: var(--font-family-sans-serif); font-size: 0.85rem; }
